    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0656" n="560" xml:id="pg560"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/1890: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Clark</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-11-01T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 1,
                                1926—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>29. Your 39, October 25, 1 p.m., paragraph 2, and Department’s 28, October 27, 1
                    p.m., paragraph 3.</p>
                <p>The Department is informed that bankers have cabled De la Rue accepting the
                    Liberian proposals regarding the assignment of revenues and the issuance of the
                    second half of the loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
